WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:11.580
[The National Tuberculosis Association presents
"Cloud in the Sky"]

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:18.360
[Director: Edgar G. Ulmer, Director of Photography:
J. Burgi Contner, Sound: Dean Cole,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:25.820
Film Editor: Marc S. Asch, Copyright MCMXXXIX by the National
Tuberculosis Association.]

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.149
[Narrator:] More than one and one half million
citizens of the United States claim Spanish

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:04.720
as their mother tongue. Their happy spirit
in the face of toil and hardship enriches

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:11.450
our land. They bear more than their share
of the crushing burden of tuberculosis. This

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:16.270
story is dedicated to them in the hope that
it will speed the day when our whole nation

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:20.350
shall be freed of man's ancient enemy, tuberculosis.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:35.400
[Music and dancing while a priest and another man look on.]

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:06.040
[Priest:] You see doctor they are a very happy
people. Their old customs, their own language,

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:13.160
all of these things mean so much to them.
They work hard, it is true, but they certainly

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.720
do enjoy themselves.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:25.140
[Doctor:] They surely do enjoy themselves.
By the way, it's late. I've got to be going.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.460
[Priest:] Well, see you again, Doctor.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.920
[Doctor:] Bye.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:36.040
[ Music and dancing continue. ]

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:44.980
[Maria whispers to Priest [inaudible] and he gets up from the table.]

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.840
[Consuelo:] Father, what is it?

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.400
[Lopez:] It is your mother.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:06.160
[Juan:] Mother had one of her coughing spells.
Blood came from her mouth.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.180
 [Inaudible] in there.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.320
[ Music ]

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:17.500
[Names of the months in Spanish flash on the
screen: Marzo, Abril, Mayo, Junio, Julio,

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.000
Agosto, Septiembre, Octubre]

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.900
[Lopez:] Why don't you eat, my child?

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.379
[Consuelo:] I'm not hungry, father.

00:03:29.379 --> 00:03:31.110
[Lopez:] You aren't sick?

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:35.509
[Consuelo:] No, don't you worry.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:47.840
[Sounds of eating and then clatter of dishes being washed.]

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:58.120
[Father is shown at workbench, repairing shoes.]

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:05.300
[Consuelo approaches her father.]

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.520
[Lopez:] I am worried, my child.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.200
[Consuelo:] Don't father...

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:16.680
[Lopez:] I can't help it. Since your mother
left [inaudible] a year ago. You have been

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:25.300
coughing. You don't eat. You feel tired. I
have watched you.

00:04:25.849 --> 00:04:31.760
[Consuelo:] I'm tired yes. Maybe I'm still
growing...wouldn't that be funny? [She coughs].

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.580
[Lopez:] There, you see.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.599
[Consuelo:] I see nothing. It hasn't rained
in so long there's dust in the road, some

00:04:37.599 --> 00:04:45.719
of it got in my throat. I won't have you worry
about me. I'm all right [cough]. 

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:53.220
It's late. You have to get up early to go to work. Good
night dearest.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:56.280
[Lopez:] Good night.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:10.539
[ Background noise ]

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:21.500
[Lopez:] Tired she was. It's not the work-
and how she coughed, just so you [inaudible].

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.800
My dear.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:46.870
[A woman is shown at a church altar. Consuelo sits in a pew. Organ music is playing. The priest looks at her.]

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:59.880
[Priest:] Consuelo, I have seen you praying. 
Peace and consolation are the blessings that

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.620
our blessed mother gives to her children.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:11.280
[Consuelo:] Father, I'm afraid. My mother
was taken from us and now I am ill.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:19.780
 I cough, I am tired all the time. I have the same signs that she had. Help me Father, help me.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.800
[Priest:] Yes, Consuelo, I will help you. I
will give you the blessings of the church

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:30.930
and all the consolations of religion, but you
must take my advice. You must go to a doctor

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.080
at once.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:39.080
He can and he will help you. You must not
use patent medicines. You must not use home

00:06:40.229 --> 00:06:46.360
remedies. God has made us to understand and
to know. He has given us an intelligence.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:53.360
He has also given us science and the doctors
spend their lives curing and helping those

00:06:54.030 --> 00:07:00.919
who are ill and who suffer. God wants us to
use the gifts that he has given us from heaven.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:02.129
You must go to a doctor Consuelo.

00:07:02.129 --> 00:07:02.379
[Doctor:] Now let's see now.

00:07:02.379 --> 00:07:02.930
[View of patient questionnaire: (n) Chronic
lower respiratory affections...none, (o) Ischio-rectal

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:03.530
abscess ..., (p) Pain... none, (q) Fever...
slight-afternoon, (r) Loss of weight (underlined)...

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:04.169
10 pounds, (s) Loss of ability to work...yes,
(t)Fatigue (underlined)... yes, (u) Sleep...,

00:07:04.169 --> 00:07:04.870
(v) Night sweats... no, (w) Confined to bed...
no, (x) Delayed recovery other illnesses...

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:04.919
no]

00:07:04.919 --> 00:07:05.470
[Next screen questionnaire continues: (a)
Cough (underlined)... slight - 5 weeks, (b)

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:11.610
Hemoptysis, date and amount... no, (c) Expectoration,
date and amount... slight, (d) Dyspnoea...

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:18.030
none, (e) hoarseness, frequent or transitory...,
(f) Chronic upper respiratory affections...,

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:25.030
(g) Sinus... normal, (h) Throat condition...
normal, (i) Teeth... ", (j) Appetite (underlined)...

00:07:25.039 --> 00:07:27.379
very poor, (k) Digestion...]

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:32.339
Now come along young lady.

00:07:32.339 --> 00:07:36.560
[ Background noise ]

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:43.560
Step up young lady, please, [your chin?].
This wonderful x-ray light goes right through

00:07:54.400 --> 00:08:01.400
your body and makes a picture of the inside
of your chest on the film. Then we can see

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:05.740
if any damage has been done to your lungs.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:12.190
With the ear we hear the sounds in the lung,
true- but the picture is even better and more

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:19.190
exact. With the x-ray we can now find tuberculosis
in the early stage before there are any other

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:27.110
signs. Step aside please.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:40.180
[ Background noise ]

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:46.120
You know Consuelo if I had my way about it
every young person, no matter how well he

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:51.750
may be would be x-rayed, that may come someday.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:58.750
[Lopez:] We do not know enough of this world
Pedro. If I only would take Consuelo's mother

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:05.610
to the doctor, but we are afraid of doctors.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:08.410
[Pedro:] How should we know, nobody tells
us.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:14.920
[Lopez:] That is what we think, but it is
not true. Men and women go around telling

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:21.920
us about the sickness. They try to explain
to us, but do we listen to them? No, we did

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:30.170
not even pay attention. Pedro, I know so well
the symptoms. Her mother had them too. Oh

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.850
I am so afraid.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:47.310
[Lopez:] I must say this is a good way to
[attend your young man?]. Am I supposed to

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.560
entertain him or what?

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.750
[Consuelo:] Why not? He's going to be around
the house if I ever marry him.

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:59.750
[Lopez:] That sounds like my Consuelo! Give
it to him. Never allow a man to be too sure.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:08.500
You look better now, I think the doctor has
helped you already but don't forget he will

00:10:12.329 --> 00:10:16.300
tell me tomorrow all about how your lungs
look.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:23.300
[Doctor:] See [Lopez?], all this is healthy
lung but there- a shadow, like a little cloud

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:29.339
in the sky. That means trouble beginning in
the lungs.

00:10:29.339 --> 00:10:36.339
[Lopez:] I suspected it- like mama, like daughter.

00:10:36.839 --> 00:10:43.839
[Doctor:] No, no tuberculosis is not inherited.
It is passed from one person to another. Now

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:47.519
let me show you what I mean.

00:10:47.519 --> 00:10:54.519
Sit down over here. The 

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:13.870
germs that cause tuberculosis grow in the
lungs of the person who has the disease. The

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:19.589
germs are very small; whoever comes close
to the mouth of the person who has tuberculosis

00:11:19.589 --> 00:11:22.279
is likely to pick up some of the germs.

00:11:22.279 --> 00:11:27.290
And once the germs are in the mouth of a healthy
person they may find their way into the lungs

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.760
-- this is how the seed of tuberculosis is
planted.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:37.760
A mother kissing her child, a sneeze or a
cough, sleeping together, sick people spit

00:11:37.889 --> 00:11:43.459
on the ground, a child later picks up the
germs on his fingers and carries them to his

00:11:43.459 --> 00:11:43.850
mouth.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:50.260
A sick person can be healed but in the meantime
he spreads the disease to many other persons

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:56.550
to whom he comes in contact. If he is cared
for in a sanatorium his diseases cannot spread.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:58.980
[Lopez:] But what can I do?

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:03.519
[Doctor:] We will send Consuelo to a sanatorium
and there she will get well.

00:12:03.519 --> 00:12:10.519
[Lopez:] Yes, I have seen them. They are beautiful,
but we are poor. Those places are for rich

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:17.019
people, not for people like us.

00:12:17.019 --> 00:12:24.019
[Doctor:] No, no they're for all. All people
in an enlightened community know that tuberculosis

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:30.870
is not only a personal misfortune but that
it threatens every household.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:36.850
Tuberculosis knows no lines of race, religion
or social status, so people gladly support

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:41.450
a sanatorium knowing that thereby their own
children will be protected.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:47.899
[Lopez:] That sounds reasonable but can my
Consuelo be taken to such a place?

00:12:47.899 --> 00:12:53.399
[Doctor:] Certainly, I will have one of the
nurses of the health department come to you

00:12:53.399 --> 00:12:56.600
and make arrangements to take Consuelo to
the sanatorium.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:58.550
[Lopez:] Thank you doctor.

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:05.550
[Doctor:] Never mind but there is one more
thing Juan and Maria must be examined also.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:12.940
Tuberculosis in its early stages is without
symptoms so don't forget to bring them here.

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:19.019
I will make a tuberculin test first and if
that shows that the germs are in their bodies

00:13:19.019 --> 00:13:25.870
then they too must be x-rayed.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:32.870
[Maria:] It didn't hurt.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:51.900
[ Background noise ]

00:13:54.430 --> 00:14:01.430
[Man:] Everybody is talking about you and
your daughter. Is she really in one of those

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:04.220
sanatoriums?

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:04.860
[Lopez:] Yes.

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.380
[Man:] And how did you do it?

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:09.589
[Lopez:] I listened and did what the doctor
told me.

00:14:09.589 --> 00:14:12.040
[Man:] I think you sold your soul to the devil.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.290
[Lopez:] What do you mean?

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:16.980
[Man:] Well, you know he can make people do
what you want them to do.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:19.370
[Lopez:] That's just exactly what I did.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.839
[Man:] You mean that?

00:14:20.839 --> 00:14:27.839
[Lopez:] Of course not, you are the most ignorant
man I ever saw. I listened and I learned and

00:14:28.769 --> 00:14:33.130
that is the trouble with you, you are ignorant
and won't learn.

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:38.930
[Man:] You're just as ignorant as I am, but
you can learn, I can learn too.

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:39.639
[Lopez:] [Hey!?]

00:14:39.639 --> 00:14:40.350
[Man:] What?

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:47.350
[Lopez:] You always spit on the floor. Of
all rotten things to do, you spit on the floor.

00:14:49.139 --> 00:14:49.649
You dumb-bell.

00:14:49.649 --> 00:14:55.250
[Man:] What is the matter with you [Lopez?].
I spit where I like, so do you.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:15:02.250
[Lopez:] I do not. I know better, let me show
what the doctor explained to me. I have a

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:08.509
book and I want you to see it yourself. Come
on.

00:15:08.509 --> 00:15:13.690
[Maria:] Consuelo, is she really going to
be well again?

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:18.149
[Nurse:] Of course she's looking splendid,
she's getting stronger every day.

00:15:18.149 --> 00:15:19.290
[Juan:] Everyday Ms. [Oleze?].

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.910
[Nurse:] Certainly, why do you ask?

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:26.509
[Juan:] She's been at the sanatorium for nearly
a year, that's a lot of days. She sure must

00:15:26.509 --> 00:15:28.130
be powerful strong by now.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:35.130
[Lopez:] Juan, you should have it all figured
out. How do you do, nurse? You are so nice

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:36.769
to come so often.

00:15:36.769 --> 00:15:41.579
[Nurse:] Well, I have to look after all of
you. Consuelo and the doctor always asks about

00:15:41.579 --> 00:15:42.019
you.

00:15:42.019 --> 00:15:49.019
[Lopez:] The children are doing fine- fresh
air, good food, plenty of rest, fresh vegetables.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.600
You see we grow them ourselves.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:58.839
[Nurse:] That's fine Mr. [Lopez?], the doctor
asked me to remind you however that it's been

00:15:58.839 --> 00:16:04.110
nearly a year since Juan and Maria were examined
and he wants you to bring them in again.

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:11.110
[Lopez:] Certainly but would you mind to come
to my home and tell me how is Consuelo?

00:16:11.509 --> 00:16:18.509
[Nurse:] That's a good girl. Well you'll be
going home soon, aren't you glad?

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:36.920
[Consuelo:] Of course but...

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:40.459
[Nurse:] But what?

00:16:40.459 --> 00:16:47.459
[Consuelo:] I don't know how I can thank all
of you.

00:16:58.079 --> 00:16:59.540
[ Pedro signing in Spanish. ]

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:06.540
[Nurse:] Oh, isn't that nice, I wonder who
it could be.

00:17:09.889 --> 00:17:16.889
[Man:] [You cannot sing you have to move on.?]

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:17.669
[ Music ]

00:17:17.669 --> 00:17:24.669
[Doctor:] Two years have passed since you
left for sanatorium. You have been a good

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:33.110
girl. I find that the lung is well-healed
now you may marry but remember...

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:51.980
[ Music ]

00:17:58.659 --> 00:18:05.659
[Priest:] Remember doctor the last time we
were here, I remarked to you that these are

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:21.899
very happy people and now I add a very healthy
people.

00:18:21.899 --> 00:18:22.179
[ Music ]

00:18:22.179 --> 00:18:27.290
[The cast, Rosario De La Vega, R. C. Ortega,
F. L. Tafolla, Frederick J. Mann, C. Ss. R.,

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.849
R. Trevino, Jr., The characters in this film
are fictitious. Any resemblance to any person,

00:18:29.849 --> 00:18:30.030
living or dead, is purely coincidental.]

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:32.369
[The generous services of friends, including
the Sidney Lanier High School, Tipica Orchestra,

00:18:32.369 --> 00:18:38.840
Works Progress Administration, and Woodmen
of the World War Memorial Hospital are gratefully

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:39.399
acknowledged.]

00:18:39.399 --> 00:18:39.969
[Music]

00:18:39.969 --> 00:18:40.539
[ Silence ]

